From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: katamaran <katamaran@localhost>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 10:30:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] forwarder: bind privileged loopback ports via lo0 on darwin

On macOS, XNU rejects unprivileged binds below port 1024 on specific
addresses such as 127.0.0.1 while allowing wildcard binds (0.0.0.0 / ::).
When binding a loopback address below port 1024 fails with EACCES, fall
back to a wildcard socket scoped to lo0 via IP_BOUND_IF/IPV6_BOUND_IF
and drop any connection or datagram whose endpoints are not loopback.
---
